nltransientdtf01.out
Time stepping by deltatfunction ends after nsteps
nltransienttransportproblem nsteps 6 deltatfunction 1 rtol 1.e-8 alpha 1. nsmax 20 nmodules 1
errorcheck
# Step n adds dt(n), first step at t=0: t = 0, 0.1, 0.2, 0.4, 0.7, 1.1.
# The dt function is defined up to step 6 only, so a step beyond nsteps
# evaluates it out of range and fails with -Werror.
# With c=0 the field is uniform and equal to the prescribed value f(t)=t.
domain HeatTransfer
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_all element_all
ndofman 6 nelem 2 ncrosssect 1 nmat 1 nbc 1 nic 0 nltf 2 nset 2
node 1 coords 3  0.0   0.0   0.0
node 2 coords 3  0.0   4.0   0.0
node 3 coords 3  2.0   0.0   0.0
node 4 coords 3  2.0   4.0   0.0
node 5 coords 3  4.0   0.0   0.0
node 6 coords 3  4.0   4.0   0.0
quad1ht 1 nodes 4 1 3 4 2
quad1ht 2 nodes 4 3 5 6 4
SimpleTransportCS 1 mat 1 set 1 thickness 0.15
IsoHeat 1 d 1. k 1. c 0.
BoundaryCondition 1 loadTimeFunction 2 dofs 1 10 values 1 1.0 set 2
PiecewiseLinFunction 1 nPoints 3 t 3 0. 3. 6. f(t) 3 0.1 0.1 0.4
PiecewiseLinFunction 2 nPoints 2 t 2 -1. 10. f(t) 2 -1. 10.
Set 1 elementranges {(1 2)}
Set 2 nodes 2 1 2

#%BEGIN_CHECK%
#NODE tStep 4 number 5 dof 10 unknown d value 4.00000000e-01
#NODE tStep 6 number 5 dof 10 unknown d value 1.10000000e+00
#NODE tStep 6 number 6 dof 10 unknown d value 1.10000000e+00
#%END_CHECK%
